 "input": "quick tour of the repo for the new dev. http handlers in api/ call the services, never the db directly. services/orders.py does order logic and uses the repo layer (repo/orders_repo.py) for SQL. payments go through services/payments.py which wraps the Stripe client, and orders calls payments.charge(). auth middleware checks the JWT on every request using the keys in config. emails are sent by a background worker reading the job queue; orders service puts \"order_confirmed\" jobs on the queue. config/ loads env vars. migrations/ holds the schema changes, repo layer depends on that schema. there's a CLI for admin tasks that also calls services.",
